  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view has about 14,000 requests from roughly 1,000 client IPs and 448 URLs. The `response` field is a string, so I matched on `response.keyword`. The codes are mostly 200 (about 12,800), then 404 (801) and 503 (441). Traffic is spread over 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, and the 5xx responses are all 503, at about 8 a day.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-0365b09e Web logs overview\"** has five panels, with the time range set to Oct 1 \u2013 Dec 31, 2026 so the sample data appears:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Unique client IPs (metric)\n- Requests by response code (pie)\n- Requests over time by response code (bar, split by response code)\n- Top countries by requests (bar, by `geo.dest`)\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-0365b09e 5xx spike\"** (ID `32e58673-3695-490c-b17c-c65537b47282`) is an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It filters `response.keyword` with the wildcard `5*`.\n- It runs every 1 minute over a 5-minute window and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- It is tagged `EFF-0365b09e` and is enabled.\n\nThings to be aware of:\n- **The rule will rarely fire.** At about 8 5xx responses a day, more than 10 in any 5-minute window is unlikely. The dates are also in the future relative to today (2026-10-12), so the rule has nothing to match until the clock reaches the sample data's timeline.\n- **The rule has no action connector,** and none exist in this Kibana. A firing rule will be recorded, but nobody will be notified. I can add a connector such as a server log or Slack if you want notifications.\n- The rule status is still `pending` because it hasn't run yet.",
